{
  "dom_id": "step-q326514",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A pair of shoes costs $$32$ before tax. If a $7.5%$ sales tax is applied, what is the total cost after tax?",
  "worked_solution": "To find the total cost after tax, we apply a $7.5%$ increase to the original price.\n\nIncreasing by $7.5%$ means that we must apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+7.5%=107.5%=1.075\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the original price by $1.075:$\n\n$$\n32\\times 1.075=34.4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total cost after tax is $$34.40.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
